{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00041 - MONDO_5224",
  "verbalization": "Aldesleukin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation through a series of molecular pathways that involve the treatment of acute myeloid leukemia. The evidence suggests that Aldesleukin is used in the management of a specific subtype of acute myeloid leukemia characterized by the T(8;16)(p11;p13) translocation, which is associated with the disease's progression. This translocation is further treated with drugs like Quizartinib, Ivosidenib, and Tioguanine, all of which are indicated for the same leukemia subtype. The integration of these pathways implies that Aldesleukin may exert its therapeutic effect through a mechanism that is linked to the treatment of this specific leukemia, potentially by modulating pathways involved in leukemia progression. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on these treatment regimens, which may indicate a broader role for Aldesleukin in the management of this disease.",
